\\neq 1.\\]\n\nThe roots of this polynomial are the 99th roots of unity, excluding 1. Therefore, the roots \\(r_1, r_2, \\ldots, r_{98}\\) are the complex numbers \\(e^{2\\pi i k / 99}\\) for \\(k = 1, 2, \\ldots, 98\\).\n\nNext, we need to evaluate the sum:\n\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{98} \\frac{r_k^2}{r_k + 1}.\\]\n\nTo proceed, we use the fact that the roots \\(r_k\\) satisfy \\(r_k^{99} = 1\\). We can rewrite each term in the sum as:\n\\[\n\\frac{r_k^2}{r_k + 1} = \\frac{r_k^2}{r_k + 1}.\n\\]\n\nTo simplify this expression, we consider the polynomial \\(P(x) = x^{98} + x^{97} + \\cdots + x + 1\\) and its roots. Notice that:\n\\[P(x) = \\frac{x^{99} - 1}{x - 1}.\\]\n\nWe need to find:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{98} \\frac{r_k^2}{r_k + 1}.\n\\]\n\nWe use the identity for the sum of the roots of unity. Consider the function:\n\\[f(x) = \\frac{x^2}{x+1}.\\]\n\nWe need to find:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{98} f(r_k) = \\sum_{k=1}^{98} \\frac{r_k^2}{r_k + 1}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use the fact that the sum of the roots of the polynomial \\(P(x)\\) taken one at a time is the coefficient of \\(x^{97}\\) divided by the leading coefficient, which is \\(-1\\). However, we need to evaluate the sum of the transformed roots.\n\nNotice that:\n\\[\n\\frac{r_k^2}{r_k + 1} = \\frac{r_k^2 + r_k - r_k}{r_k + 1} = r_k - \\frac{r_k}{r_k + 1}.\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{98} \\frac{r_k^2}{r_k + 1} = \\sum_{k=1}^{98} \\left( r_k - \\frac{r_k}{r_k + 1} \\right).\n\\]\n\nThe sum of the roots \\(r_k\\) is \\(-1\\) (since the sum of all 99th roots of unity is 0, and excluding 1 leaves \\(-1\\)). Therefore:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{98} r_k = -1.\n\\]\n\nWe need to evaluate:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{98} \\frac{r_k}{r_k + 1}.\n\\]\n\nUsing the symmetry and properties of roots of unity, we know:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{98} \\frac{r_k}{r_k + 1} = 49.\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{98} \\frac{r_k^2}{r_k + 1} = -1 - 49 = -50.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-50}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-50}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
